// axis-wireframe's `.ax`-facing surface. Deliberately thin: the actual
// capability (a live-settable `wireframe` property) lives entirely in
// extension.js and needs no AXIS-level helper at all - `box.wireframe =
// true` inside an `on` handler already works once the extension's own
// script has registered it. This export exists so a consuming `.ax` file
// has something to `import` at all: AXIS has no side-channel "just
// install this extension" mechanism (deliberately - see
// docs/runtime-extensions.md) - a package only ever activates because
// some `.ax` source actually imports it, the same rule as every other
// AXIS package, runtime-extension-carrying or not.
export fn toggleWireframe(obj) {
    obj.wireframe = !obj.wireframe
}
